.SH NAME
ktm-map \- Hash tables, and ordered maps (red-black trees).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import map;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Hash tables, and ordered maps (red-black trees).
.SH TYPES
.SS Entry
.EX
struct Entry<K, V> {
    K key;
    V value;
    u64 hash;
    bool live;
};
.EE
.PP
---- the map ---- Entries are kept in insertion order in \fBentries\fR; \fBslots\fR is the hash table, each slot the index of an entry (EMPTY, or GONE after a delete so probe chains stay whole). Rebuilt when the slots are 3/4 used.
.SS Map
.EX
struct Map<K, V> {
    Entry<K, V> *entries;
    i64 nentries;
    i64 entcap;
    i64 *slots;
    i64 nslots;
    i64 len;
};
.EE
.SS TreeNode
.EX
struct TreeNode<K, V> {
        K key;
        V value;
        i64 color;
        TreeNode<K, V> *left, *right, *parent;
};
.EE
.SS Tree
.EX
struct Tree<K, V> {
        TreeNode<K, V> *root;
        TreeNode<K, V> *nil;
        i64 len;
};
.EE
.PP
nil is the tree's own black sentinel (made by the first set), the leaf every path ends in: the only node whose left is null
